 "structural_finding": "The nadir footprint scales with depth; the threat cylinder does not. The footprint half-width reaches the 12 m threat radius only at 19.5 m (along-track) / 26.0 m (cross-track) depth, both far outside the +/-6.0 m vertical threat band. Inside the band the camera images at most 9.04 % of the cylinder's cross-section (at 6 m below), and 4.02 % at this encounter's 4.03 m separation. Birds ABOVE the drone (dz > 0, half the band) are behind a nadir camera and are structurally unimageable. This is a sensor-horizon-vs-policy-horizon mismatch, not a detector sensitivity problem.",
